Tripe isn't all that rare. It often can be conveniently found in a shop.
When you make an effort to collect the randomly generated tripe before
your pet can, you'll often find at least one for every shop in the
first levels. Used right, one tripe ration is sufficient to _empty_ one
shop (or even more than one) very quickly.
Using a whistle (BTW, magic whistles _are_ quite rare on the first
levels) you have to wait until your pet grabs an item, move away and try
to whistle your pet out of the shop. In that time, the pet will often
have dropped the item (having low apport). You have to repeat that for
_every_ item you want. Maybe I'm doing it wrong, but *I* find that far
less effective than a trained pet.

